      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"body\":\"## Problem Statement\\n\\nThe four core transaction modules \u2014 POS, Repairs, Orders, and Quotes \u2014 each implement their own customer selection logic, line item validation schemas, and UI components independently. This creates duplication (~150-200 lines of near-identical search/debounce/dropdown code per module), inconsistent behavior (customer required in some modules but optional in others), and makes cross-module changes error-prone because the same concept is implemented differently four times.\\n\\nPOS currently only supports parts-only line items, making it unable to serve as a reference implementation for the other three modules which already support labor and bicycle line types. The validation schemas are scattered across separate files with no shared variant definitions, meaning any change to how a \\\"part\\\" or \\\"labor\\\" line item works must be replicated manually in up to four different schema files.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nMake POS the clean reference implementation by:\\n1. Extracting the customer selector into a single shared component used by all four modules\\n2. Creating shared line item variant definitions that each module composes into its own validation schema\\n3. Upgrading POS to support all three line item types (part, labor, bicycle) matching the domain model already present in the database\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. As a cashier using POS, I want to select an existing customer or leave it blank for walk-in sales\\n2. As a cashier using POS, I want to add parts from catalog via barcode scan or search\\n3. As a cashier using POS, I want to create special (ad-hoc) products when item not in catalog\\n4. As a cashier using POS, I want to add labor services with hourly time tracking\\n5. As a cashier using POS, I want to add bicycle line items referencing templates\\n6. As a repair technician, I want optional customer on repair intake for walk-in repairs\\n7. As a repair technician, I want CRUD line items on repairs incrementally\\n8. As a salesperson, I want optional customer on orders for walk-in orders\\n9. As a salesperson, I want atomic parts/labor/bicycle line items when creating order\\n10. As a salesperson, I want optional customer on quotes for anonymous estimates\\n11. As a salesperson, I want CRUD line items on quotes incrementally\\n12. As a developer, I want shared CustomerSelector component used by all modules\\n13. As a developer, I want shared line item variant definitions in one file\\n14. As a shop owner, I want every part sold to reference catalog entry\\n\\n## Implementation Decisions\\n\\n### Module 1: Shared Customer Selector Component (Frontend)\\n- Extract from POS into `client/src/features/customers/components/CustomerSelector.tsx`\\n- Props: `{ customerId?: string | null, onSelect, required?: boolean }`\\n- All four modules import and use this component\\n\\n### Module 2: Shared Line Item Variant Definitions (Shared Validations)\\n- Create `shared/validations/line-item-variants.ts` with part/labor/bicycle variants\\n- Each module composes its own discriminated union from shared variants\\n\\n### Module 3: Customer Optional Across All Modules (Backend Schemas)\\n- Repairs: allow customerId null without existing/new customer path\\n- Orders: customerId changed to nullable optional\\n- POS/Quotes already optional \u2014 no change\\n\\n### Module 4: POS Service Layer Upgrade (Backend)\\n- `createDirectSale()` handles labor and bicycle line items\\n- Stock validation only on part-type items\\n\\n### Module 5: POS Cart Store Upgrade (Frontend)\\n- Cart supports discriminated union of all three line item types\\n- Cart display renders appropriate fields per type\\n\\n## Testing Decisions\\n\\n1. Shared Customer Selector \u2014 unit tests for selection callback, null handling\\n2. Line Item Variant Schemas \u2014 unit tests for each variant valid/invalid inputs\\n3. POS Sales Service \u2014 integration tests: parts-only, labor, bicycle, mixed-type cart\\n4. Orders Schema \u2014 unit test customerId optional\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n1. Line item UI components (parts/labor/bicycle sections) \u2014 deferred to later pass\\n2. Fixed-price labor services \u2014 hourly stays core\\n3. Bicycle inventory management \u2014 templates only\\n4. Inline customer creation at POS \u2014 walk-in only\\n5. Multi-payment split, invoicing, void auth guard\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[PRD] Cross-Module Generalization: Customer Component + Full POS Line Items\"}\n"
      }
    ],
